        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk5-manner-reference-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Refer back to an established manner or degree",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "This formal reference points back to a manner or degree supplied by context. Without that referent, it does not tell the reader what the manner is. 如此 can also precede an adjective to mark that degree or a verb phrase to refer to that manner. Its antecedent must be recoverable.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他每天读书，我也如此。",
                "pinyin": "tā měitiān dúshū ， wǒ yě rúcǐ 。",
                "meaning": "He reads every day, and so do I.",
                "audio": "efd609e7166b8ce32edaa6d1ff73fd835ea0070d9403bdb9a3ebdb5452c4a4b8"
              },
              {
                "text": "他非常认真，我也想如此认真。",
                "pinyin": "tā fēicháng rènzhēn ， wǒ yě xiǎng rúcǐ rènzhēn 。",
                "meaning": "He is very conscientious, and I too want to be that conscientious.",
                "audio": "55e98ad5ba9962e291146644d070902cd97ba5b13d2d1029d68ae39088c91313"
              },
              {
                "text": "老师先听后说，我们也如此做。",
                "pinyin": "lǎoshī xiān tīng hòu shuō ， wǒmen yě rúcǐ zuò 。",
                "meaning": "The teacher listens first and speaks afterward; we do it that way too.",
                "audio": "5d51c5f46773b19d579e54c982ce09d9e0c00816b1b77f7ead7efc38be88d83d"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
